Despite appearances, those aren't drinks.

152
00:12:14,780 --> 00:12:17,140
Madam, please, you have to listen to me.

153
00:12:17,400 --> 00:12:18,880
My, what is it?

154
00:12:20,180 --> 00:12:22,920
Well, uh, it's about Miss Holly.

155
00:12:23,460 --> 00:12:24,290
Oh!

156
00:12:24,373 --> 00:12:26,677
Look at this Japanese
man's unique fashion sense!

157
00:12:26,760 --> 00:12:27,720
Very nice!

158
00:12:28,240 --> 00:12:29,600
Hi there, how are you?

159
00:12:29,780 --> 00:12:32,020
Give me a big smile if you would! Huh?

160
00:12:32,400 --> 00:12:33,877
What the hell are you doing, lady?

161
00:12:33,960 --> 00:12:36,640
Who gave you permission
to videotape me, huh?

162
00:12:38,040 --> 00:12:39,517
Please, madam, get in the car.

163
00:12:39,600 --> 00:12:40,600
Nice to meet you.

164
00:12:40,780 --> 00:12:42,057
Come back here, dammit!

165
00:12:42,140 --> 00:12:43,260
We're not done!

166
00:12:43,580 --> 00:12:46,277
I'll be taking that camera
from you before you leave!

167
00:12:46,360 --> 00:12:47,737
Who do you think you are?

168
00:12:47,820 --> 00:12:49,537
You're just a damn foreign hag!

169
00:12:49,620 --> 00:12:51,837
You're looking to see some
blood today, you rich bitch?

170
00:12:51,920 --> 00:12:52,750
Huh?

171
00:12:52,833 --> 00:12:54,480
All right, that's enough.

172
00:12:54,840 --> 00:12:57,600
I forbid you to lay
another finger on Madam.

173
00:13:01,180 --> 00:13:04,437
Madam, you should try learning a
bit more about Japanese culture.

174
00:13:04,520 --> 00:13:05,350
Okay.

175
00:13:08,620 --> 00:13:10,020
I couldn't do it.

176
00:13:10,240 --> 00:13:13,297
I couldn't tell her Miss Holly
only has a few days left.

177
00:13:13,380 --> 00:13:14,777
It would break her heart.

178
00:13:14,860 --> 00:13:17,801
And that's the last thing
I would ever want to do.

179
00:13:32,560 --> 00:13:35,560
We've almost arrived, and
I still haven't told her.

180
00:13:35,880 --> 00:13:37,762
I can't put this off any longer.

181
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:40,440
We'll soon be in sight of the Kujo house.

182
00:13:41,060 --> 00:13:43,060
She needs to hear this from me.

183
00:13:47,240 --> 00:13:48,080
It's okay.

184
00:13:48,440 --> 00:13:51,087
I know there's something
you want to tell me.

185
00:13:51,240 --> 00:13:53,240
You don't need to pretend anymore.

186
00:13:53,520 --> 00:13:56,226
I'm well aware of what's
troubling you, Roses.

187
00:13:56,380 --> 00:13:59,204
My daughter's life is in
grave danger, isn't it?

188
00:14:06,580 --> 00:14:09,000
I called Holly from New York a few times.

189
00:14:09,140 --> 00:14:12,857
She put on a brave face and
pretended to be cheerful and lively.

190
00:14:12,940 --> 00:14:16,440
She tried her best to convince
me it was only a mild cold.

191
00:14:17,260 --> 00:14:18,577
Whenever Joseph phoned,

192
00:14:18,660 --> 00:14:21,317
he would tell me his business
trip kept him very busy,

193
00:14:21,400 --> 00:14:23,635
but that I had nothing to worry about.

194
00:14:24,340 --> 00:14:27,693
But I knew they were keeping
something important from me.

195
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:32,237
Deep down, I knew something terrible was
happening to my daughter and husband.

196
00:14:32,320 --> 00:14:35,057
I've been married to
Joseph for 50 years now,

197
00:14:35,140 --> 00:14:38,020
and my sweet Holly is
my own flesh and blood.

198
00:14:39,440 --> 00:14:43,637
I never pressed them for more information
because I was afraid of what they'd say.

199
00:14:43,720 --> 00:14:46,857
I wanted nothing more than
to see my precious daughter.

200
00:14:46,940 --> 00:14:50,352
But the thought of what I'd
find here was almost too much!

201
00:14:51,160 --> 00:14:54,517
You know this much, so you also
have the right to know the rest.

202
00:14:54,600 --> 00:14:57,737
As it stands, your daughter only
has a few days left to live.

203
00:14:57,820 --> 00:14:58,940
That's why Mr.

204
00:14:59,080 --> 00:15:02,397
Joestar and the others went to Egypt
To end the source of her illness?

205
00:15:02,480 --> 00:15:05,040
But there's been no news for a while.

206
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:09,997
Please, can you find it in your heart
to forgive me for not telling you?

207
00:15:10,080 --> 00:15:14,257
There was nothing we could do for Miss Holly
so I wanted to spare you from the pain,

208
00:15:14,340 --> 00:15:15,170
but I was wrong.

209
00:15:15,253 --> 00:15:16,317
I should have told you.

210
00:15:16,400 --> 00:15:18,100
It was cruel of me not to.

211
00:15:19,780 --> 00:15:23,133
I don't want to hear any more
of that foolishness, Roses.

212
00:15:23,420 --> 00:15:27,891
No matter how grim things seem, there's
still one thing we can do for Holly.

213
00:15:50,360 --> 00:15:51,580
Hi, sweet girl.

214
00:16:00,080 --> 00:16:02,380
I'm so glad you're here.

215
00:16:03,660 --> 00:16:05,860
Listen to me very carefully, Roses.

216
00:16:06,200 --> 00:16:10,024
Right now, the one thing we can
do for my daughter is have faith.

217
00:16:11,140 --> 00:16:15,560
I don't understand everything that's
happening, but here's what I do know.

218
00:16:15,980 --> 00:16:17,860
Joseph and my grandson, Jotaro,

219
00:16:18,160 --> 00:16:21,217
are putting their lives on the
line in the hope of saving Holly.

220
00:16:21,300 --> 00:16:24,300
And I believe they will
find a way to do just that.

221
00:16:24,460 --> 00:16:25,720
He's never failed me.

222
00:16:25,920 --> 00:16:28,317
Not once in the 50 years I have known him.

223
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:31,997
He's kept every promise he's made
since the two of us met in Italy.

224
00:16:32,080 --> 00:16:36,727
Once he's made up his mind to do something,
nothing in this world can stop him.

225
00:16:37,980 --> 00:16:40,509
Rest and believe in
Jotaro and your father.

226
00:16:40,920 --> 00:16:45,626
You'll be better before you know it, and
our family will be together once again.

227
00:16:45,980 --> 00:16:47,280
Thank you, Mama.

228
00:16:50,640 --> 00:16:54,640
Madam Joestar, Miss Holly,
please hang in there.

229
00:17:09,120 --> 00:17:13,680
That cool ice, Billy
Jean, even Darby Younger.

230
00:17:14,380 --> 00:17:17,280
I knew they were nothing
but incompetent fools.

231
00:17:25,440 --> 00:17:30,560
I shouldn't laugh, but knowing they got
what they deserve feels so satisfying.

232
00:17:31,980 --> 00:17:34,657
That's what the fools get
for calling me a loser.

233
00:17:34,740 --> 00:17:38,300
But at least now we know
I wasn't one after all!

234
00:17:38,880 --> 00:17:40,080
Don't be absurd.

235
00:17:40,420 --> 00:17:44,037
You can't possibly defeat the
Joestars using that pathetic power.

236
00:17:44,120 --> 00:17:45,414
Out of the way, loser.

237
00:17:45,700 --> 00:17:47,280
Hey, but that's not fair!

238
00:17:47,540 --> 00:17:49,540
I want a chance to fight them too!

239
00:17:49,940 --> 00:17:52,060
You're merely an ordinary vampire.

240
00:17:52,520 --> 00:17:55,917
You'd best stay out of our way
or we might end up killing you!

241
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:58,540
Do try to behave yourself, loser.

242
00:18:01,880 --> 00:18:04,292
I'll be the one who finishes off Jotaro!

243
00:18:10,680 --> 00:18:11,510
Stop!

244
00:18:11,640 --> 00:18:14,052
There's something up ahead, to the right!

245
00:18:24,400 --> 00:18:25,360
A woman.

246
00:18:27,160 --> 00:18:28,920
Please have mercy on me!

247
00:18:29,120 --> 00:18:30,340
I'm begging you!

248
00:18:30,460 --> 00:18:31,636
Don't suck my blood!

249
00:18:31,740 --> 00:18:32,820
Anything but that!

250
00:18:34,780 --> 00:18:36,860
I swear I'll do whatever you want.

251
00:18:37,080 --> 00:18:38,140
Just let me live.

252
00:18:38,300 --> 00:18:39,594
That's all I'm asking.

253
00:18:40,880 --> 00:18:42,600
Hey, easy now.

254
00:18:42,820 --> 00:18:44,114
You need to calm down.

255
00:18:44,400 --> 00:18:45,960
I won't run away anymore.

256
00:18:46,160 --> 00:18:47,420
You can trust me.

257
00:18:47,680 --> 00:18:48,739
Please have mercy.

258
00:18:49,020 --> 00:18:49,850
Just breathe.

259
00:18:49,933 --> 00:18:52,777
We aren't Dio's minions, and
we're certainly not vampires.

260
00:18:52,860 --> 00:18:54,080
We're the good guys.

261
00:18:54,520 --> 00:18:56,820
So just calm down and let us help you.

262
00:18:57,580 --> 00:18:58,680
You're good guys?

263
00:19:00,220 --> 00:19:01,200
Good guys?

264
00:19:01,600 --> 00:19:03,977
You're really not those evil vampires?

265
00:19:04,060 --> 00:19:06,957
You're actually going to
help me get away from here?

266
00:19:07,040 --> 00:19:08,900
That's right. We're good.

267
00:19:14,460 --> 00:19:17,260
Real good at punching evil in the face.

268
00:19:19,220 --> 00:19:22,102
If you still want help,
we'll be happy to oblige.

269
00:19:22,240 --> 00:19:25,077
We'll help by sending you
on a one-way trip to hell.

270
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:26,400
Sound good, Kakyoin?

271
00:19:30,800 --> 00:19:31,630
Help!

272
00:19:31,880 --> 00:19:35,180
Damn it! Help! Tell me! Help! Help!

273
00:19:36,020 --> 00:19:37,820
How did you figure it out?

274
00:19:38,040 --> 00:19:40,400
My power is impossible to crack!

275
00:19:40,740 --> 00:19:42,597
Would this power have anything to do with

276
00:19:42,680 --> 00:19:44,697
the face of a woman on
the back of your head?

277
00:19:44,780 --> 00:19:46,717
For future reference,
when you flip your head,

278
00:19:46,800 --> 00:19:49,271
you should make sure your hands match too.

279
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:53,680
Shit! You're right!

280
00:19:53,900 --> 00:19:55,000
I never noticed!

281
00:19:55,200 --> 00:19:56,140
I'm an idiot!

282
00:19:57,140 --> 00:19:58,437
No, you're a loser.

283
00:19:58,520 --> 00:20:00,820
Now where is Dio's room? Out with it.

284
00:20:01,880 --> 00:20:03,717
Jotaro, try not to knock him unconscious.

285
00:20:03,800 --> 00:20:05,094
He can take us to Dio.

286
00:20:06,380 --> 00:20:07,760
How dare you!

287
00:20:08,060 --> 00:20:09,317
Don't you call me that!

288
00:20:09,400 --> 00:20:13,165
You're just like those other guys,
so you'll meet the same fate!

289
00:20:13,920 --> 00:20:15,140
I'll kill you!

290
00:20:15,440 --> 00:20:17,499
Lord Dio's powers made me immortal!

291
00:20:17,680 --> 00:20:20,268
And I'll use all of it
to rip you to pieces!

292
00:20:23,940 --> 00:20:27,297
So unless I heard wrong, you
just said you were an immortal.

293
00:20:27,380 --> 00:20:29,340
So you're a vampire like Dio.

294
00:20:30,120 --> 00:20:31,280
In which case,

295
00:20:31,500 --> 00:20:35,617
I can use you as a practice dummy for
when I fight against the real thing.

296
00:20:35,700 --> 00:20:36,960
Oh my god!

297
00:20:48,900 --> 00:20:50,780
So you really are immortal.

298
00:20:51,280 --> 00:20:52,162
Vampire or not,

299
00:20:52,280 --> 00:20:55,917
we can still rip you into little pieces
and scatter them around the room.

300
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:58,257
Well, are you taking us to Dio or not?

301
00:20:58,340 --> 00:21:00,080
The sun is about to set.

302
00:21:00,540 --> 00:21:04,180
Okay, but can I at
least ask you one thing?

303
00:21:04,780 --> 00:21:08,898
How the hell did you know the other
stand users used to call me loser?

304
00:21:10,040 --> 00:21:11,700
Oh man, good grief.

305
00:21:34,880 --> 00:21:36,540
Thank you.

306
00:22:10,040 --> 00:22:12,440
Thank you.

307
00:22:49,060 --> 00:22:50,660
I gotta hand it to him.

308
00:22:51,220 --> 00:22:53,338
Dio's got some pretty nice curtains.

309
00:22:57,100 --> 00:22:58,020
All right.

310
00:22:58,340 --> 00:23:01,222
Now I can walk and even
jump around if I need to.

311
00:23:01,400 --> 00:23:05,753
It still hurts a bit, but now's not
the time to worry about a little pain.

312
00:23:15,580 --> 00:23:16,677
Greetings, Polareff.

313
00:23:16,760 --> 00:23:18,300
What a pleasant surprise.

314
00:23:20,800 --> 00:23:22,320
Dio, at last.

315
00:23:26,820 --> 00:23:28,620
You've finally come out, Dio.

316
00:23:28,860 --> 00:23:30,500
I knew this day would come.

317
00:23:30,700 --> 00:23:32,520
I have absolutely no regrets.

318
00:23:32,840 --> 00:23:34,917
There's something you need to hear first.

319
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:36,577
Is he playing games with us?

320
00:23:36,660 --> 00:23:38,542
When did he bring out his stand?

321
00:23:38,840 --> 00:23:40,840
I'll give you a chance to rethink.
